invariant: INV-46
file: src/mlkem_lanes.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-vector
reason: the SSE2 message expansion gives lane j the bit 7 - j of its byte,
  so each byte's eight coefficients come out in the reverse order and an
  encapsulation encrypts another message. bin/mlkem_vector_equiv_test runs
  every byte value at every position through both expansions. Only an
  x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds the test for
  x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and
  this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    __m128i bits = _mm_setr_epi16(1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128);
--- new
    __m128i bits = _mm_setr_epi16(128, 64, 32, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1);
